[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/dialogue/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n1_hugh"
text = "# DRAFT
# Prior Hugh at dusk on the north walk (night 1). Cold; he suspects the new porter from the first.
# He asks why a country house sent a boy to keep a London gate (n1_hugh_why), then gives his rule:
# nobody comes in after the curfew bell without the prior (n1_hugh_rule).
# If the porter drank hard at the Keys he says so. hangover is cleared by the day-1 nap, so n0_saw_killing=drunk is the real test.
== start
(A tall brother stands in the middle of the north walk, hands in his sleeves, watching you come.)
Hugh: The new porter. I am Hugh, prior of this house.
-> keys [if hangover]
-> keys [if n0_saw_killing=drunk]
-> why

== keys
Hugh: You came to us from the Cross Keys this morning smelling of it. I noticed. So did others.
-> why

== why
Hugh: A small house in the country sends a boy of nineteen to keep a gate in London. Why you?
* My abbot sent me, and I came. -> obedient
* There was no one else to send. -> nobody
* Why does it matter to you? -> matters

== obedient [set n1_hugh_why=obedient] [trust hugh 5]
Hugh: Obedience. Keep some by you. You'll need it here.
-> rule

== nobody [set n1_hugh_why=nobody]
Hugh: That I believe.
-> rule

== matters [set n1_hugh_why=matters] [trust hugh -5]
Hugh: Everything that comes in at that gate matters to me. You came in at it.
-> rule

== rule [set n1_hugh_rule]
Hugh: Hear the one rule I care about. After the curfew bell, nobody comes in at that gate unless I say so.
Hugh: Pilgrim, priest or the King's own uncle. You send for me, and you wait.
-> end

== again
Hugh: You've had your rule, porter. Go to your supper.
-> end

== leave
Hugh: After the bell, porter. Remember.
"
